# FORCED arms (no shipped DBAR): the GRNT section arms of DestructibleBarrier (REL 13), which need a
# GRNT script connection to a generated script object. 08_sand_casualpirates (42b935e4) has 79 SCGN
# objects; 00360244 is a CScriptDebris, 00360245 a CScriptPickup. The player stands at (355.43,
# -240.26, 3.79) and the barriers at the same height, chunks 1.0 high (the SLdr default), 5 hp each:
# `damage 6` with the player teleported to a chunk's height destroys exactly that chunk (TakeDamage's
# actor arm aims at the damage source's position).
# A (e0036ff00): 1x1x10, a non-GRNT connection before the GRNT one; five hits from the top down give
# five split-offs, the fifth past the four-section cap. B (e0036ff01): 1x1x6 to the pickup, which the
# console deletes (PreRender/RenderChunks meet the gone actor before Think drops the section). C
# (e0036ff02): GRNT to an editor id with no SCGN entry (GenerateScriptObject returns no object). D
# (e0036ff03): 1x1x10, two split-offs in one tick: `damage` only queues the Damage message (a second
# `damage` in the tick adds to the same hit), so `send Damage` runs TakeDamage at once and the second
# split finds the generated sfx already played. E (e0036ff04): no base/full-row/full-layer model, in
# view and never damaged (RenderChunks' null-model arms). The damage radius is 20, so the player is
# teleported next to C and D.
# Run: BUILD=build-port-cov tools/cov/run.sh tools/cov/specs/destructiblebarrier.py <out> \
#   42b935e4,08_sand_casualpirates --con tools/drivers/destructiblebarrier_grnt.con --fast --frames 1000
